  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#41928\", \"PowerToys#36956\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. PowerToys#41928 is the same Command Palette problem: subtracting two close, large numbers gives a result with extra digits. In that ticket, 3033554.11 - 3033359.71 gave a long decimal instead of 194.40. The cause is IEEE 754 binary floating-point error. The calculator shows 15 significant digits, so the error is visible. The result is not a wrong calculation. The ticket's suggested fix is to lower the displayed precision to about 10–12 digits, but the archive doesn't show that it has been released. PowerToys#36956 describes similar subtraction noise in the PowerToys Run calculator. For now, round the result yourself, for example 0.68099999999993 is 0.681. Please add your examples (615.419-614.738 and 616.686-615.158) and your version, 0.100.2, to PowerToys#41928. Please don't file a new ticket.\"}",
